## 🏗️ Architecture Overview

### The Strict 5-Layer Pattern

Every request follows this exact flow:

```
1. ROUTE
   ↓
2. CONTROLLER
   ↓
3. SERVICE
   ↓
4. QUERY (Repository)
   ↓
5. DATABASE / SEED
```

### Layer Responsibilities

| Layer | Does | Never Does |
|-------|------|-----------|
| **Route** | Maps URL → Controller | Contains logic, DB calls |
| **Controller** | Parses request → Calls service → Returns response | Business logic, DB access |
| **Service** | All business logic, DB/Cache/Seed decisions | HTTP stuff, direct DB calls |
| **Query** | Fetches data from DB/Seed only | Business logic |
| **Model** | Defines schema structure | Contains logic |

### Example Flow

```javascript
// 1. REQUEST ARRIVES
GET /api/users/123

// 2. ROUTE MATCHES
app.get('/api/users/:id', controller.getUser);

// 3. CONTROLLER HANDLES
async getUser(req, res) {
  const user = await userService.getUser(req.params.id);
  return response.success(res, user);
}

// 4. SERVICE DECIDES
async getUser(id) {
  // Check cache first
  const cached = await cache.get(`user:${id}`);
  if (cached) return cached;
  
  // Try database
  try {
    const user = await userQuery.getById(id);
  } catch(err) {
    // Fallback to seed
    const user = await seedProvider.getUser(id);
  }
  
  // Cache and return
  await cache.set(`user:${id}`, user, 3600);
  return user;
}

// 5. QUERY FETCHES DATA
async getById(id) {
  const user = await User.findById(id);
  if (!user) throw new Error('Not found');
  return user;
}

// 6. DATABASE RETURNS
User: { _id: '123', name: 'John', email: '...' }

// 7. CACHE STORES
Cache: user:123 → { _id: '123', ... } (TTL: 3600s)

// 8. RESPONSE SENT
{ success: true, data: { _id: '123', name: 'John', ... } }
```

