## 🔍 Debugging Common Issues

### Issue: No DB Connection, Not Using Seed
**Solution**: Ensure database.js has try-catch and seed provider is initialized
```javascript
try {
  await db.connect();
} catch(error) {
  logger.warn('Using seed data fallback');
}
```

### Issue: Cache Not Working
**Solution**: Verify Redis connection and cache layer in service
```javascript
const cached = await cache.get(key);
if (!cached) {
  const data = await query.fetch();
  await cache.set(key, data, ttl);
}
```

### Issue: Controllers Have Business Logic
**Solution**: Move all logic to service layer
```javascript
// Move this from controller to service
const processed = data.map(d => d * 2); // ❌ In service
const filtered = data.filter(d => d.active); // ✅ In service
```

### Issue: Direct DB Calls in Multiple Places
**Solution**: Centralize all DB access in query layer
```javascript
// Use this everywhere
const user = await userQuery.getById(id);

// Never this
const user = await User.findById(id);
```

### Issue: Inconsistent Response Format
**Solution**: Always use response helper
```javascript
// ✅ Consistent
return response.success(res, data);
return response.error(res, message);
return response.paginated(res, data, page, limit, total);

// ❌ Inconsistent
return res.json({ data });
res.send(data);
res.status(200).json(data);
```

